    "S.16 shipped-conformance section6 explicitly permits a transitional opt-in plaintext debugging override. Broad purpose-level no-opt-out wording must not erase that exception.",
    "Tier1 has no forward secrecy against node-key compromise. Request encryption does not establish response protection, executor blindness, metadata privacy, key rotation or Tier2 compliance.",
